7592186158378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157527 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157527 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Exponential Equations Using the Zero-Product Property" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157527 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186158376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157527 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157527 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186157527 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "986c9303-5c90-5d19-85f8-915c37c8bfb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158376 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158376 #edb/ref 1061 467336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158376 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "56edca54-b7a1-571d-b42c-21eaa3456fa1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158376 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186158530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158377 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186158378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158377 #edb/ref 1061 467337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158377 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f532c29e-5c06-5b5f-8c3b-8a42ad9ae43e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158377 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158378 #edb/ref 1061 467340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158378 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "942b92f8-26b9-51c3-94de-c738c9f145af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158378 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186157438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158530 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we want to find all of the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\nx \\cdot 3^x - 2 \\cdot 3^x = 0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot {3}^{x}-2\\cdot {3}^{x} & =0 \\\\ (x-2)\\cdot {3}^{x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\nx-2  = 0 \\quad \\textrm{and} \\quad 3^x=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation $x-2=0$ has the solution $x=2.$\n\n- The equation $3^x=0$ has no real solution because $3^x$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has a single solution, $x=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158530 #edb/ref 1065 4715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158530 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "90c9dc44-008d-5e8d-b233-b33802547a9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186158530 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172023 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048784 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172023 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172023 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172023 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186237896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172023 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172023 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172023 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172023 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172023 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Roots of a Transformed Radical Function With an Odd Index" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172023 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186171829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172023 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "3e6159dd-c12e-5882-be17-815b4cc9ae52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172024 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172024 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172024 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172024 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186237900 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172024 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186292704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172024 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172024 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172024 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175